course: dictionary
lesson: 290
title: Amphipods: small shrimp-like animals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scientists often learn a new word from the clues around it. «Amphipods are small shrimp-like animals in the deepest trenches that eat dead stuff sinking from above.» The words small and shrimp-like tell you what an amphipod looks like, and eat dead stuff tells you what it eats.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. An amphipod is a small shrimp-like animal with no shell on its back, such as the sand hopper found on beaches. Does «Amphipods are small shrimp-like animals» still make sense? Yes, so your meaning fits.
explain: Amphipods live in different places. The science phrase «freshwater amphipod» tells you some live in fresh water, while sand hoppers live on beaches. The word is a noun, so you can say an amphipod or some amphipods.
fact: An amphipod is a small shrimp-like animal with no shell on its back.
fact: A sand hopper is one kind of amphipod, and it is found on beaches.
fact: «Amphipods» live in the deepest trenches, where they eat dead stuff sinking from above.
fact: Scientists have found plastic inside some amphipods, so plastic can reach even the deepest parts of the sea.
fact: Amphipods are a common invertebrate, so you will meet them in lessons on minibeasts, rock pools and food chains.
exercise: «Amphipods are small shrimp-like animals in the deepest trenches.» What are amphipods? | Birds that eat plastic | Plants that grow in deep trenches | Large animals with thick shells | *Small shrimp-like animals
exercise: A sand hopper is one kind of amphipod. Where might you find one? | On the moon | In a school desk drawer | Inside a volcano | *On a beach
exercise: The sentence says amphipods eat dead stuff sinking from above. Where does that stuff come from? | From inside the amphipods | From the bottom of the trench | From the sand on the beach | *From above, sinking down through the water
test: What does an amphipod have no shell on? | Its tail | Its legs | *Its back | Its eyes
test: Which phrase names an amphipod that lives in fresh water? | A deep trench | *A freshwater amphipod | A food chain | A rock pool crab
exam: Based on the sentence, what do amphipods eat? | Living fish hidden in the sand | Rocks and shells | Plastic only | *Dead stuff sinking from above
